//@version=6
// ── PARITY-EXPORT BUILD (VWAP) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// Instrumented build used ONLY to validate the Python port (engines/vwap/) against this Pine source.
// It reproduces the single VWAP line from mpc_assistant.pine — `vwapValue = ta.vwap(hlc3)` (line
// 852) — and emits the columns the Python compare tool needs:
//
//   px_volume       — the bar's volume (the input Python's engine is fed; guarantees both sides use
//                     the exact same volume series, so there is no data-source mismatch).
//   px_vwap         — ta.vwap(hlc3), the ground-truth session VWAP value to diff against.
//   px_vwap_anchor  — the trading-day roll pulse (1 on the first bar of a new "D" bar). ta.vwap's
//                     default anchor is the start of the trading day, i.e. THIS boundary; it is the
//                     CALIBRATION signal for the Python --htf-tz / --htf-rollover, exactly like the
//                     liquidity export's px_day_roll.
//
// Export on the SAME chart/timeframe you run the Python compare on (e.g. VANTAGE_XAUUSD, 5m), Export
// chart data → CSV, and diff with engines/vwap/tools/compare_vwap.py. Do NOT let the logic drift.
indicator("VWAP Engine EXPORT", overlay = false)

// Ground-truth VWAP — identical to mpc_assistant.pine line 852.
vwapValue = ta.vwap(hlc3)

// Trading-day boundary (ta.vwap's default anchor). Same "D" security roll the liquidity export uses.
[dTime] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", [time], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
dayRoll = dTime != dTime[1]

c0 = color.new(color.gray, 100)
plot(volume,               "px_volume",      c0)
plot(vwapValue,            "px_vwap",        c0)
plot(dayRoll ? 1 : 0,      "px_vwap_anchor", c0)
